      "content": "Please do not give your 6-year-old adult aspirin; aspirin can cause Reye's syndrome, a serious condition in children. For fever and discomfort, it is much safer to use children's acetaminophen (like Tylenol) or ibuprofen, dosing according to his weight and age. If his symptoms worsen, he becomes lethargic, or you are concerned, please contact your pediatrician right away.",
